  "title": "The body and daily routine",
  "note": "With body parts French uses le, la, les rather than my or your: Je me lave les mains. Avoir mal à says what hurts: J'ai mal à la tête, au dos, aux pieds. Routine verbs are reflexive and take a pronoun that matches the subject: je me lève, tu te lèves, il se lève, nous nous levons.",
